# Phase 132.0: every window this scenario can open, by screenshot, in day
# mode and then in night vision. Not a pass/fail check on its own: the
# shots are what tests\ui-baseline.ps1 compares, before and after a UI
# change, to show which windows the change touched.
#
# Jupiter fills the object and info panels with something real. The GoTo
# panel is shown, not toggled. HELP and AI are toggles, pressed once on
# the assumption that a fresh sandbox starts with them hidden; the first
# -Save run on the rig confirms it (the report lists every window it
# found). The sky map and telemetry windows come up with the workspace.
# What matters for the diff is that both runs show the SAME windows,
# which the noise run checks. Modal dialogs are
# not opened: a modal would stop the scenario, and they are named in the
# phase document as not covered.
#
# Shot names must not contain '_': ShotDiff splits the file name there.
name    UI baseline: every window, day and night
timeout 240

expect 30  Started -- EMULATOR
expect 30  [SCENARIO] UI baseline
wait   4
goto   Jupiter
expect 120 Slew to 'Jupiter' complete
press  GOTO
press  HELP
press  AI
wait   4
shot   day
key    N
expect 5   [NIGHT] Night Vision ON
wait   3
shot   night
key    N
expect 5   [NIGHT] Night Vision OFF
wait   1
